From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:56:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: sun6i-dma: Complete the channel that raised the
 interrupt

The interrupt handler reads one status register per group of
num_channels_per_reg channels, but picks the physical channel by the
bit position inside the register alone. An interrupt of a channel in
register i > 0 is matched against the channel at the same position in
register 0.

On the A733 every channel has a status register of its own
(num_channels_per_reg is 1), so the interrupts of channels 1 to 15 are
all taken for channel 0: a transfer on any other channel never
completes, and a transfer on channel 0 can be completed by the
interrupt of another channel. On controllers with 16 channels in two
registers the same happens to channels 8 to 15.

Index the channel by register and bit, the same way
sun6i_dma_start_desc() picks the register and the bit for a channel.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; dmatest with 1000
copies on each of 17 channels at once ends with 0 failures and no
timeout.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/dma/sun6i-dma.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/dma/sun6i-dma.c b/drivers/dma/sun6i-dma.c
index 2d23be1a67f1..db4946947b5b 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/sun6i-dma.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/sun6i-dma.c
@@ -603,7 +603,8 @@ static irqreturn_t sun6i_dma_interrupt(int irq, void *dev_id)
 		sun6i_write_irq_stat(sdev, i, status);
 
 		for (j = 0; (j < sdev->cfg->num_channels_per_reg) && status; j++) {
-			pchan = sdev->pchans + j;
+			pchan = sdev->pchans +
+				i * sdev->cfg->num_channels_per_reg + j;
 			vchan = pchan->vchan;
 			if (vchan && (status & vchan->irq_type)) {
 				if (vchan->cyclic) {
